> You sit. The crate wobbles. So does his, in sympathy.
@if var.homeword == "smell"
    charlie: I picked the vent on purpose. Laundry soap. You said. I've been sitting in your answer for ten minutes.
@elif var.homeword == "people"
    charlie: You said home was "whoever's still up." So. I'm still up. I'm the most up anyone has ever been.
@elif var.homeword == "place"
    charlie: You said home was a window. So I found you one. Third floor, across the street. Yellow curtain. Light's been on since I got here.
    charlie: I've decided someone in there is reading a very good book. I've decided it's your window now.
@else
    charlie: I picked the warm spot. The vent. It smells like clean laundry. Tell me that's not a home.
@if charlie.romance >= 4
