@else
    > He holds out a can of hot chocolate from the machine downstairs. He's got one for himself, too.
    charlie: I didn't know what you drink, so I got what I'd want. That's how I buy everyone presents. It works about sixty percent of the time.
@if flag.cold
    charlie[smile]: Also, Hamin-hyung said you were cold earlier. He told me to tell you the vent is warm. He was very specific about it.
> Below, the laundromat dryers are still turning. Somewhere, a delivery scooter goes by, and then the street is quiet again.
charlie[thinking]: So. Not fate.
charlie: I really wanted it to be. In the archive. I asked out loud, in front of everyone. Songha-hyung made his spreadsheet face.
charlie: Because if it's fate, then it's not an accident that I keep ending up in places. Somebody meant it. There's a reason.
charlie[smile]: But it wasn't. It was just you, being in airports. And me, being in airports. And both of us noticing.
charlie: Which is kind of better? It means we picked it. You can't pick fate. You *can* pick a sofa.
* [sincere] "I'd rather be picked than planned."
    @rel charlie trust+1 romance+1
