> In the east, over the low roofs toward the river, the sky is starting to think about getting lighter.
charlie[thinking]: Hey. Your letter said "a place you want to stay."
charlie: I'm not saying I'm a place. I'm not a place. I'm a guy on a crate.
charlie[smile]: But if you ever want to stay somewhere for a bit, as a trial, I'm very easy to stay with. I leave the kitchen light on. It's a whole policy.
