@show charlie laugh at=c
charlie: Okay. Deliveries. From the group. I'm the postman. The postman is also staying for lunch.
> He unpacks them onto the floor like a very proud magician.
charlie: From Hanbi-hyung: a phone charger. He says everyone always forgets, and you'll need one here.
charlie: From Songha-hyung: a label maker. He's already labelled it. It says LABEL MAKER.
charlie[smile]: From Haruta-hyung: a plant. There was a note. "I chose this one myself." He underlined "myself" twice.
charlie[laugh]: And from Daniel-hyung: this dinosaur. He says he won it. He did not win it. Justin-hyung saw him buy it.
> You hold up an unopened box of snacks with a sticky note on top, in Hyunjun's handwriting: *half of these were for you. justin ate the other half.*
charlie: That's accurate. I watched it happen.
> You put the kettle on. He argues, seriously and at length, about which cupboard the mugs belong in. He loses. He moves them anyway, when he thinks you're not looking.
charlie[thinking]: Oh. Last thing. This one's from me.
> It's the photograph, printed, a little grainy. The amber board. Every DELAYED. A hand in the corner, pointing at a gate.
> He sticks it to your fridge with a magnet shaped like a slice of toast, and steps back, and nods at it.
charlie[smile]: There. Now you're from here. It's on the fridge. That's legally binding.
* [playful] "Is that how it works?"
    charlie[laugh]: That's exactly how it works. Ask any fridge.
* [sincere] "Thank you. It looks right there."
    charlie[shy]: …Yeah. It does. I thought it would. I was a bit nervous it wouldn't.
* [quiet] Stand next to him and look at it for a while.
    > He leans a little into your shoulder, the way people lean on a fence they trust, and doesn't say anything for almost a whole minute. A personal record.
> When he finally leaves, it's dusk. You walk him to the door.
> On the way out, without saying anything, he reaches past you and switches on the kitchen light.
charlie: Policy.
> The door closes. The light stays on. It buzzes, just a little, like a fridge having thoughts.
@end
